ops.argument	Match the arguments to `foundation --help` or `foundation <operation> --help`
ops.unknown-operation	Use a name from `foundation --help`
ops.input	Give standard input a source that can be read
ops.output	Give standard output a destination that can be written
ops.bad-plan	Make a plan with `foundation plan`, and apply it with no edits
ops.behind	Fix the cause, then plan again
ops.stale-plan	Plan again
ops.apply	Fix the cause in the message, then plan and apply again
ops.stopped	Fix the cause in the message, then start the node and plan again
ops.bad-request	Use a `foundation` program of the same version as the node
ops.denied	Ask an admin of the region for an access policy that allows it
ops.large-reply	Plan and apply the change in smaller steps
ops.channel-read	Fix the cause in the message, then ask for the status again
ops.read	Fix the cause in the message, then run the command again
ops.write	Give `--out`, or `out` of the MCP tool, a path in a directory that can be written
ops.large-request	Make the config files smaller
ops.bad-reply	Use a `foundation` program of the same version as the node
ops.outside	Give a path under one of those folders. A relative path is relative to the working directory /work. To reach another folder, add `--files <DIR>` to the command of the MCP server
ops.hidden	Give a path outside /work/foundation-data
ops.plan-name	Give `out` a path that ends in `.plan` and is not a link to another file
ops.wide-folder	Add `--files <DIR>` for each folder that the tools may read and write
ops.folder	Give `--files` a folder that is there
ops.data	Make /work, or give `--data` a directory whose parent is there
ops.unknown-extension	Use a file that ends in `.hcl`
ops.path-not-utf8	Rename the file to a UTF-8 name
secret.unresolved	Give the node the value at the source, or change the source, then plan again
